WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.820
Treat JWT handling as a security

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.333
boundary with an explicit acceptance
policy.

3
00:00:05.333 --> 00:00:08.233
A readable payload is merely decoded
input.

4
00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:11.423
Base64url encoding is not encryption, and
a successful

5
00:00:11.423 --> 00:00:14.323
signature check is not complete token
validation.

6
00:00:14.323 --> 00:00:17.416
The verifier must use trusted key material
and

7
00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:20.703
enforce the algorithm family configured
for the issuer.

8
00:00:20.703 --> 00:00:23.893
Issuer and audience answer different
questions: who issued

9
00:00:23.893 --> 00:00:27.276
the assertion, and which recipient should
accept it.

10
00:00:27.276 --> 00:00:28.243
Validate both.

11
00:00:28.243 --> 00:00:31.046
Require expiration for access tokens,
respect not-before

12
00:00:31.046 --> 00:00:34.042
restrictions, and use only justified clock
tolerance.

13
00:00:34.042 --> 00:00:36.942
Issued-at records issuance time rather
than expiry.

14
00:00:36.942 --> 00:00:39.746
A JWT identifier can support tracking, but

15
00:00:39.746 --> 00:00:42.646
its presence alone does not prevent
replay.

16
00:00:42.646 --> 00:00:44.385
Keep token purposes distinct.

17
00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:47.962
Access tokens belong at their intended
APIs; refresh tokens

18
00:00:47.962 --> 00:00:51.635
belong in the refresh flow with stronger
lifecycle controls.

19
00:00:51.635 --> 00:00:55.695
Other signed token classes must meet their
own acceptance rules.

20
00:00:55.695 --> 00:00:58.885
Key selection is also constrained:
token-provided identifiers can

21
00:00:58.885 --> 00:01:01.688
select candidates within trusted
configuration, never establish

22
00:01:01.688 --> 00:01:04.975
a new key source or trigger arbitrary
retrieval.

23
00:01:04.975 --> 00:01:08.648
In Express, verify first, validate
required runtime claim shapes

24
00:01:08.648 --> 00:01:12.418
and meanings, and then create the minimum
authenticated context.

25
00:01:12.418 --> 00:01:15.318
TypeScript types do not perform those
checks.

26
00:01:15.318 --> 00:01:17.541
Authentication precedes object, tenant,
scope,

27
00:01:17.541 --> 00:01:19.861
role, ownership, and business
authorization.

28
00:01:19.861 --> 00:01:23.341
Decide how fresh authorization state must
be for each

29
00:01:23.341 --> 00:01:27.014
operation instead of assuming signed
claims remain current indefinitely.

30
00:01:27.014 --> 00:01:29.141
Operational controls complete the design.

31
00:01:29.141 --> 00:01:32.234
Protect browser storage and transport
according to the

32
00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:35.521
threat model, keep credentials out of
telemetry, and

33
00:01:35.521 --> 00:01:39.097
plan refresh, key rotation, revocation,
and dependency failures.

34
00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:43.157
Local logout is not automatic invalidation
of all issued tokens.

35
00:01:43.157 --> 00:01:46.830
Test rejected tokens and denied access
alongside successful requests.

36
00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.310
Trust a JWT only after the server has
verified

37
00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.500
who protected it, confirmed that it was
issued

38
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.077
for this application and purpose,
established that it is

39
00:01:57.077 --> 00:02:00.267
currently valid, and translated its claims
into the

40
00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:03.940
minimum authenticated context needed for a
separate authorization decision.

